The new briefing is intended to be stateless/read-only, but it invokes a Git command that can write repository metadata and fail under read-only or locked-index conditions. That violates a load-bearing contract of the change.

Review comment:

- [P2] Avoid refreshing the index in the read-only briefing — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-t1c/scripts/steward-orient.sh:134-134
  When the index stat cache is stale, `git status` refreshes and may rewrite `.git/index`, which violates this script's stated “writes nothing” contract; in a read-only checkout or while another process holds the index lock, this can also make the briefing exit because the pipeline runs under `pipefail`. Use `git --no-optional-locks status ...` or `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0` for this dirty-count probe.
